Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:59:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test(#622): pins for pole clicks snapping the roll to the
 nearest quarter turn

Red on main: toward([0,0,1]) reads atan2(0,0)=0 whatever the pre-click
yaw, and basis_right's pole guard pins screen-right to literal +X, so a
TOP/BOT click spins the model up to half a turn on screen. These pins
demand the snap law: yaw to the nearest FRAC_PI_2, right (-sin y, cos y,
0) at the pole, post-click up within 45 degrees of pre-click up, and a
second pole click that changes nothing. Decision in
docs/decisions/622-viewcube-roll-snap.md.
